false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"They almost do.\n\nI have a Python callback that creates a `np.random.default_rng` with the current PRNGKey I am using in the jax function in order to have deterministic RNG across the Python/jax boundary.\n\nUnfortunately, `default_rng` fails with jax arrays. (It's probably a bug on their end, but still, as you documented the callback to always return numpy arrays...)","created_at":"2022-09-02T10:24:33Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/12194#issuecomment-1235330789","id":1235330789,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/12194","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5Joabl","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":1,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1235330789/reactions"},"updated_at":"2022-09-02T10:24:53Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1235330789","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2407108?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/PhilipVinc","id":2407108,"login":"PhilipVinc","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MDcxMDg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PhilipVinc","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59483310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/becker63","id":59483310,"login":"becker63","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NDgzMzEw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/becker63","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-05-21T15:08:53Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"OWNER","body":"## Purpose\n\nEstablish **parallel-owner** issues so agents/subagents can work without collapsing SearchBench vs IC vs MCP vs evaluator causality. Tracks follow **Game → Round → Match → Evidence → Decision** vocabulary.\n\n**Recent context:** work on **`main`** (diagnostic rounds under `configs/rounds/diagnostic-*`; IC submodule MCP tolerating **`query`/`symbol`** aliases; matrices / live-matrix debugging docs) surfaced asymmetric tool ergonomics, harness quirks (evaluator fields affecting policy systems; Buck pinning **`liveconfig.RoundID`**; **`live_smoke`** proof semantics differing from **`evaluate_n`**).\n\n## Proof pathways (aggregate)\n\nChild issues (**#115**–**#119**) each lock a **narrow knob** plus a **`README.md`** contract for what success means. Taken together they do **not** prove “everything works end-to-end”—they constrain **what class of defect** survives after you walk specific evidence paths.\n\n### Graph (lanes → cumulative read)\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TB\n  subgraph Structural[\"Structural / resolver + identity\"]\n    D115[[\"#115 Evaluator ↔ policy resolution\\n(fake eval · live JM+IC)\"]]\n    D116[[\"#116 Manifest id ↔ bundle_path / report IDs\"]]\n  end\n\n  subgraph Ops[\"Operational signals\"]\n    D117[[\"#117 Matrix taxonomy + evaluator NDJSON\\n(live cerebras evaluator)\"]]\n  end\n\n  subgraph Sandbox[\"IC sandbox\"]\n    D118[[\"#118 IC MCP anchor\\n(stub incumbent · fake eval)\"]]\n  end\n\n  subgraph Modes[\"Mode teaching\"]\n    D119[[\"#119 Buck mode vs proof freshness\\n(same manifest)\"]]\n  end\n\n  D119 -->|\"caveat: semantics\"| D115\n  D119 -->|\"caveat: semantics\"| D116\n  D115 -->|\"if clean\"| AGG[[\"Epic aggregate:\\ninfra vs resolver vs IC-only\"]]\n  D116 -->|\"if clean\"| AGG\n  D117 -->|\"signals bucket\"| AGG\n  D118 -->|\"isolates IC path\"| AGG\n```\n\nLinks in the graph are **epistemic hints** (“first read `:live_smoke` vs `:evaluate_n`” from **#119** changes how sharp **#115**/**#116** diffs feel), not prerequisites for running rounds.\n\n### Certainty tiers (what is definitive vs exploratory)\n\n| Tier | Role | Issues | Bundle / evidence anchor | Considered definitive when… |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **A — Structural invariant** | SearchBench merges ids / policy systems correctly for the manifest knobs under test | **#115**, **#116** | Canonical **`…/rounds/*-001/`** dirs + **`validate_bundle`** | Checklist fields in child **`README`** match manifests (`resolved-round.json`, `spec.policies`, `report.round_id`, path segments)—no unexplained bleed or substitution (**#116**: no stray **`liveconfig.RoundID`**). |\n| **B — Telemetry / taxonomy** | Classify **`stderr`/bundle** bursts into comparable buckets across parallel matches | **#117** | Single-plane **`diagnostic-issue-117-matrix-trace-001/`** + matrix **`evidence/matrix/**`** attempts | **`evaluate_matrix_*` + **`SEARCHBENCH_BUNDLE_EVALUATOR_TRACE`** reproduces labelled prefixes + **`bundle/observability/*.ndjson`** suitable for scripted bucketing (see **`live-matrix-debugging.md`**). |\n| **C — IC sandbox + semantics teaching** | Isolate IC MCP without incumbent JM MCP load; clarify mode-driven proof shape | **#118**, **#119** | **`diagnostic-issue-118-ic-anchor-001/`** · **`diagnostic-issue-119-proof-modes-001/`** ⚠ | **#118**: anchor NDJSON / **`failures.challenger`** as controlled IC baseline—not a full production proof. **#119**: **`report.mode`** / rollup differences demonstrate mode semantics (**same dirname rewired across runs** → snapshot before crossing modes). |\n\n### Example composed pathways (non-exhaustive)\n\n| Path expectation | Signals you combine | If it holds… | If it conflicts… |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Harness layering sound for knobs under test** | **#115** clean + **#116** identifiers match **`round.pkl`** ids | Prefer blaming live providers/MCP flakes or matrix capacity—not silent resolver/id skew for those scenarios | Re-open **resolver** (**#115**) vs **CLI identity** (**#116**) lanes before tuning agents |\n| **Matrix logs are truthful; failure is infra/tooling** | **#117** shows expected aggregates + evaluator traces bucket correctly; **live-ic-vs-jcodemunch** still rejects | Confidence triage artefacts are calibrated; escalate provider/MCP payloads or dataset rows cited in summaries | Inspect matrix skip/cache semantics (`--matrix-force`) before trusting aggregate-only reads |\n| **IC-specific ergonomics baseline** | **#118** reproduces IC fallout with stub incumbent | Narrow IC MCP / challenger schema work without full incumbent MCP surface area | Contrasts with broad **#115** failures ⇒ avoid single-cause (“evaluator bleed only”) closures |\n| **`:live_smoke` vs `:evaluate_n` artefact deltas are understood** | **#119** + child **`README`** target choice | Artefact deltas map to **`ModeLiveSmoke`/multi-attempt** semantics—not silent corruption | Prefer **`:evaluate_n`** for coupling bugs flagged in **#115**/`AGENTS.md` |\n\nFull per-issue proof text + commands stay in **`configs/rounds/diagnostic-issue-* /README.md`**. Operational greps hub: **`src/docs/reference/live-matrix-debugging.md`**.\n\n## How to delegate (parallel-friendly)\n\nPick **one numbered sub-issue** — avoid mixing unrelated layers in a single PR. Prefer **Buck targets** (`AGENTS.md`) for reproducible bundles.\n\n### Workstreams (see child issues)\n\n1. Resolver semantics in SearchBench Go (**evaluator vs policy systems**).\n\n2. Buck bundle identity **`RoundID`** for non-live round manifests.\n\n3. Failure taxonomy in reports / stderr for triage.\n\n4. iterative-context deterministic fuzzy anchor / richer primitives.\n\n5. Diagnostics + docs (**`live_smoke`** caveats vs **`evaluate_n`**).\n\n## Children\n\n_Linked individually; use Project fields or assign owners per lane._\n\n<!-- SEARCHBENCH_BUNDLE_BLOCK_V1 -->\n\n### Bundle roots + `:validate_bundle` (child issues landed on `main`)\n\n| Issue | Canonical single-plane **`…/games/code-localization/rounds/`** dirname | Offline validation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| #115 | `diagnostic-issue-115-eval-scope-001/` | `buck2 run '//configs/rounds/diagnostic-issue-115-evaluator-scope:validate_bundle'` |\n| #116 | `diagnostic-issue-116-round-bundle-001/` | `buck2 run '//configs/rounds/diagnostic-issue-116-round-bundle-id:validate_bundle'` |\n| #117 | `diagnostic-issue-117-matrix-trace-001/` (matrix leaves also **`evidence/matrix/`**) | Wired `:validate_bundle` covers `_BUNDLE_PATH` only → use **`searchbench buck validate-bundle --bundle-path=…`** for matrix attempts (**`AGENTS.md`**) |\n| #118 | `diagnostic-issue-118-ic-anchor-001/` | `buck2 run '//configs/rounds/diagnostic-issue-118-ic-anchor:validate_bundle'` |\n| #119 | `diagnostic-issue-119-proof-modes-001/` (⚠ rewired between modes) | `buck2 run '//configs/rounds/diagnostic-issue-119-proof-modes:validate_bundle'` |\n\nFull proofs + artefacts live beside each **`round.pkl`** in **`README.md`**. Docs hub: **`src/docs/reference/live-matrix-debugging.md`** (*GitHub epic repro rounds* row).\n","closed_at":"2026-05-22T04:19:27Z","comments":7,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/issues/114/comments","created_at":"2026-05-19T23:55:04Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/issues/114/events","html_url":"https://github.com/becker63/searchbench-go/issues/114","id":4481957888,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/issues/114/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOSL964M8AAAABCyVAAA","number":114,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/issues/114/reactions"},"repository":{"allow_forking":true,"archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/{archive_format}{/ref}","archived":false,"assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/assignees{/user}","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/git/blobs{/sha}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/branches{/branch}","clone_url":"https://github.com/becker63/searchbench-go.git","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/collaborators{/collaborator}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbench-go/comments{/number}","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/becker63/searchbe